.TH SWIFT-OBJECT-RELINKER "1" "December 2017" "OpenStack Swift"

.SH NAME
\fBswift\-object\-relinker\fR \- relink, cleanup, and audit objects for partition power increases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swift\-object\-relinker
[\fIoptions\fR] <\fIcommand\fR>

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The relinker prepares an object server's filesystem for a partition power
change by crawling the filesystem and linking existing objects to future
partition directories. If requirements outside the operator's control forced
a partition power increase to be marked finished before cleanup completed, it
can also audit old partition directories and quarantine stale hashes that
would otherwise result in consistency-engine warnings or dark data.

More information can be found at
.BI https://docs.openstack.org/swift/latest/ring_partpower.html

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBrelink\fR
Relink files for partition power increase.

.TP
\fBcleanup\fR
Remove hard links in the old locations.

.TP
\fBaudit\fR
Recover from a prematurely finished partition power increase by immediately
quarantining stale hash directories left in old locations. Audit is not a
normal post-cleanup step and is not intended for use immediately after
cleanup. The finished ring does not identify the affected policy, so the
\fB\-\-policy\fR option is required. When auditing a replicated policy, stop
\fBobject\-replicator\fR before starting audit, keep it stopped until audit
completes, and then restart it. Otherwise, primary peers may restore a stale
hash directory after audit quarantines it, preventing audit from making
lasting progress. With an erasure-coded policy, lone stale fragments instead
produce reconstructor errors when peers cannot provide enough fragments to
rebuild them. Those failures prevent the stale fragments from becoming fully
rebuilt, durable dark data.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message and exit

.TP
\fB\-\-swift-dir\fR \fISWIFT_DIR\fR
Path to swift directory

.TP
\fB\-\-devices\fR \fIDEVICES\fR
Path to swift device directory

.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fIPOLICY\fR
Policy name or index to process; may be specified multiple times. This option
is required for \fBaudit\fR. By default, \fBrelink\fR and \fBcleanup\fR process
all policies.

.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-mount\-check\fR
Don't test if disk is mounted

.TP
\fB\-\-max\-audit\-history\-quarantine\-threshold\fR \fIN\fR
Allow \fBaudit\fR to quarantine a hash directory only when its current
location is an ancestor within the most recent \fIN\fR partition power
increases. The value must be between 1 and 32 inclusive; the default is 2.

.TP
\fB\-\-logfile\fR \fILOGFILE\fR
Set log file name

.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable debug mode

.SH DOCUMENTATION
.LP
More in depth documentation in regards to
.BI swift\-object\-relinker
and also about OpenStack Swift as a whole can be found at
.BI http://docs.openstack.org/developer/swift/index.html
and
.BI http://docs.openstack.org
